  "parentQA": [
    {
      "q": "Who answers at 2 a.m.?",
      "a": "Jack, then Ryan. Both have Eli's number. No account manager, no call center. We stay mid-size so he's never in a bigger client's shadow."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do fees work?",
      "a": "Capped by the NFLPA and put in writing before anything is signed. Nothing up front, and nothing on money he never receives. We'll go through the exact terms in person."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do you protect what he earns?",
      "a": "Ryan writes the guarantee and injury language. We screen every advisor before he meets them, coordinate taxes, set up disability insurance and build a year-one budget. A good first contract is only the start."
    },
    {
      "q": "What happens if he gets hurt?",
      "a": "Injury settlements, grievances and second opinions are ours to handle. Disability coverage is in place before the first snap."
    },
    {
      "q": "What if he's not drafted where we hope?",
      "a": "We've placed undrafted free agents who are still in the league. The slot decides the first contract; preparation decides the second. ElevaTE makes year one count in any round."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are you, really?",
      "a": "35 years and six clients who became the highest paid at their position. Jack played the position; Ryan is a licensed attorney. Call any current client's parent; we'll give you the numbers."
    }
